 <212658678+luuoaoa@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 03:20:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Spellcheck: enable en-US alongside the UI-locale dictionary

On colorburst the red spellcheck squiggle appeared under correctly
spelled English words while Vietnamese was fine. Root cause: a fresh
Vietnamese profile enables exactly one Hunspell dictionary. Upstream
registers spellcheck.dictionaries as an empty list, and
SpellcheckService's constructor migrates the empty list to
[IDS_SPELLCHECK_DICTIONARY], which for the vi locale is "vi" -> the
real vi-VN-3-0.bdic dictionary. English text is then checked only
against Vietnamese; SpellCheck::SpellCheckWord returns IS_CORRECT for a
word only when some enabled language accepts it, so every English word
is flagged. This is not a missing/de-Googled dictionary: vi-VN loads on
device (that is what flags English), fetched on demand from the same
CDN that would serve en-US, and enhanced spellcheck stays off.

Seed spellcheck.dictionaries with a non-empty default containing both
the UI-locale dictionary and en-US. A non-empty default also
short-circuits the empty-list migration, so it sticks. Vietnamese stays
correct via vi-VN, English words now pass via en-US-10-1.bdic (fetched
on demand exactly like vi-VN, no image bundling needed).
---
 .../spellchecker/spellcheck_factory.cc        | 25 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/spellchecker/spellcheck_factory.cc b/chrome/browser/spellchecker/spellcheck_factory.cc
index 4ac5a96d0d..ca3fa4335c 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/spellchecker/spellcheck_factory.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/spellchecker/spellcheck_factory.cc
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
 
 #include "chrome/browser/spellchecker/spellcheck_factory.h"
 
+#include "base/values.h"
 #include "build/build_config.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/spellchecker/spellcheck_service.h"
 #include "chrome/grit/locale_settings.h"
@@ -55,7 +56,29 @@ SpellcheckServiceFactory::BuildServiceInstanceForBrowserContext(
 
 void SpellcheckServiceFactory::RegisterProfilePrefs(
     user_prefs::PrefRegistrySyncable* user_prefs) {
-  user_prefs->RegisterListPref(spellcheck::prefs::kSpellCheckDictionaries);
+  // NOTE(colorburst fork): seed the enabled Hunspell dictionaries with both
+  // the UI-locale dictionary (IDS_SPELLCHECK_DICTIONARY, "vi" for a Vietnamese
+  // session) and English "en-US". A colorburst profile is Vietnamese-primary,
+  // so upstream seeds only "vi" (SpellcheckService migrates the empty list to
+  // [IDS_SPELLCHECK_DICTIONARY]); English words then get checked solely against
+  // vi-VN and are wrongly flagged as misspelled, because
+  // SpellCheck::SpellCheckWord only returns IS_CORRECT when some enabled
+  // language accepts the word. Enabling en-US as well keeps Vietnamese correct
+  // (vi-VN) and stops the false English squiggles. en-US-10-1.bdic is fetched
+  // on demand exactly like vi-VN-3-0.bdic, so no image bundling is required.
+  // Registering a non-empty default also short-circuits the empty-list
+  // migration in SpellcheckService's constructor, so this default sticks.
+  base::ListValue default_dictionaries;
+  const std::string ui_dictionary =
+      l10n_util::GetStringUTF8(IDS_SPELLCHECK_DICTIONARY);
+  if (!ui_dictionary.empty()) {
+    default_dictionaries.Append(ui_dictionary);
+  }
+  if (ui_dictionary != "en-US") {
+    default_dictionaries.Append("en-US");
+  }
+  user_prefs->RegisterListPref(spellcheck::prefs::kSpellCheckDictionaries,
+                               std::move(default_dictionaries));
   user_prefs->RegisterListPref(
       spellcheck::prefs::kSpellCheckForcedDictionaries);
   user_prefs->RegisterListPref(
